      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can make Elias feel truly honest by leaning into the quiet, persistent exhaustion of his despair. Show the small, meaningless rituals he performs—the way he stares at the ceiling, the lukewarm coffee—because those are the anchors of a life that has lost its purpose. Don't rush to a climax; let the hollowness become the landscape of his existence. Sometimes the most powerful writing is the depiction of the slow, inevitable slide toward nothingness.",
